sentences.l:
Senseless indeed and worthless is that man,
whoever to his host strife brings forward over contests
in a foreign land;

for exceedingly, in an unseemly way, I was subdued
in many waves, since not tending on board the ship
was never-failing;

being angry because this man in the gathering, standing by you,
reviled you, in which way your excellence no mortal would find fault with,
whoever knew in his own wits how to speak what is fitting;

But when he had fashioned the trick, angry with Ares,
he set out to go to the chamber, where for him his dear bed lay,
and about the bedposts poured the bonds in a circle all round;

and many too from above from the roof-beam had been poured down,
like spider-webs, thin, which no one could even see,
not even of the blessed gods;
